          "guid": "mryyhd5frvnmz04k",
          "message": {
            "text": "Deliberate deviation from the ticket's item 3, flagged for review. DM-1772 says \"switch the whole-run fallback from composeStatesFlipbook to full chrome demotion.\" Taken literally (drop the flipbook), that regresses the DM-1764 guarantee that autoCompress never grows output: chrome demotion (the chrome union) only beats the flipbook when states share subtrees the union deduplicates. For a PURE wholesale slideshow the union can't dedupe and comes out slightly larger than the flipbook (measured on the DM-1764 fixture: demoted 10.7 KB vs flipbook ~9.9 KB).\n\nSo instead of replacing the flipbook, the guard keeps it as a third candidate and emits the real-bytes minimum of {keep-all, per-region demotion, flipbook floor}. This honors the maintainer's chosen per-region rule (\"minimize bytes\") AND preserves never-worse-than-uncompressed. Chrome demotion still wins where the ticket measured it (the mixed fixture, 81.8 < 97.8). If the maintainer prefers the literal item-3 (accept the pure-wholesale regression), dropping the composeStatesFlipbook candidate here is a one-line change.\n",
            "markdown": "**Deliberate deviation from the ticket's item 3**, flagged for review. DM-1772 says \"switch the whole-run fallback from `composeStatesFlipbook` to full chrome demotion.\" Taken literally (drop the flipbook), that regresses the DM-1764 guarantee that `autoCompress` never grows output: chrome demotion (the chrome union) only beats the flipbook when states share subtrees the union deduplicates. For a PURE wholesale slideshow the union can't dedupe and comes out slightly larger than the flipbook (measured on the DM-1764 fixture: demoted 10.7 KB vs flipbook ~9.9 KB).\n\nSo instead of *replacing* the flipbook, the guard keeps it as a third candidate and emits the real-bytes minimum of {keep-all, per-region demotion, flipbook floor}. This honors the maintainer's chosen per-region rule (\"minimize bytes\") AND preserves never-worse-than-uncompressed. Chrome demotion still wins where the ticket measured it (the mixed fixture, 81.8 < 97.8). If the maintainer prefers the literal item-3 (accept the pure-wholesale regression), dropping the `composeStatesFlipbook` candidate here is a one-line change.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
