          "guid": "mryyhdawdwpjqr5d",
          "message": {
            "text": "The preRun snapshot must be taken BEFORE the keep-all compose, not inside the guard. manageFonts:false means keep-all's PUA / dmfN addressing is appended to the shared builder and left live. Each per-region trial below snapshots AFTER keep-all and restores, so it leaves keep-all's addressing intact for the next trial. But if a demoted (or flipbook) candidate wins, it must become the REAL output owning the addressing — so we restoreGeneration(preRun) to undo keep-all entirely, THEN re-compose the winner. Without the pre-keep-all snapshot there'd be no marker to roll keep-all back to, and the winner's addressing would stack on top of keep-all's, shifting the real output's bytes. The tests/compress-size-guard.e2e.test.ts mixed-fixture byte-identity assertion (re-compose === compose) pins that this lifecycle leaves no trace.\n",
            "markdown": "The `preRun` snapshot must be taken BEFORE the keep-all compose, not inside the guard. `manageFonts:false` means keep-all's PUA / `dmfN` addressing is appended to the shared builder and left live. Each per-region trial below snapshots AFTER keep-all and restores, so it leaves keep-all's addressing intact for the next trial. But if a demoted (or flipbook) candidate wins, it must become the REAL output owning the addressing — so we `restoreGeneration(preRun)` to undo keep-all entirely, THEN re-compose the winner. Without the pre-keep-all snapshot there'd be no marker to roll keep-all back to, and the winner's addressing would stack on top of keep-all's, shifting the real output's bytes. The `tests/compress-size-guard.e2e.test.ts` mixed-fixture byte-identity assertion (re-compose === compose) pins that this lifecycle leaves no trace.\n"
          },
